.TH AIWG 1 "January 2026" "aiwg 2026.01.0" "AIWG Manual"
.SH NAME
aiwg \- Agentic AI Workflow Guide CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aiwg
[\fIcommand\fR]
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aiwg
is a modular toolkit for AI-powered SDLC, marketing, and content workflows.
It provides specialized AI agents, workflow commands, and templates for
software development lifecycle management, marketing campaigns, and content
creation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B auth login [--device]
Authenticate for paid AIWG web resources using browser PKCE or a device code.
.TP
.B auth status [--json]
Show account, scope, plan, expiry, and credential-store metadata without tokens.
.TP
.B auth logout [--all]
Revoke authorization and remove local credentials.
.TP
.B use \fIframework\fR
Deploy a framework to the current project. Available frameworks: sdlc, marketing, all.
.TP
.B list
List installed frameworks and their status.
.TP
.B remove \fIid\fR
Remove an installed framework.
.TP
.B mcp serve
Start the MCP server for tool integration.
.TP
.B mcp install \fItarget\fR
Install MCP config for a target (claude, cursor).
.TP
.B mcp info
Display MCP server information.
.TP
.B cost-report --fleet [--source openrouter] [--config fleet.yaml] [--json]
Observe per-bot OpenRouter month-to-date spend and correlate generation IDs
recorded in the local AIWG activity log. AIWG observes spend; OpenRouter
enforces key limits and caps.
.br
Use B--key key_refR for a single referenced key without a fleet file.
.TP
.B effect id \fIidentity\fR
Print the effect ID for an identity (\-\-kind, \-\-target, context flags, or
\-\-review, \-\-continuation and \-\-proposal\-version for a D13 review).
.TP
.B effect intent \fIidentity\fR \fIpayload\fR
Append a signed intent record before the effect. The payload is given as
\-\-payload\-file or \-\-payload\-digest and is recorded as a digest only.
.TP
.B effect record \fIidentity\fR \fIpayload\fR [--unverified]
Record and sign an effect in one command: intent, verify and completed.
Repeating it with the same payload returns the existing receipt.
.TP
.B effect lookup \fIeffect-id\fR|\fIidentity\fR
Report everything recorded for an effect ID.
.TP
.B effect reconcile \fIeffect-id\fR|\fIidentity\fR
Ask the kind's verifier again and append a reconciled record.
.TP
.B effect probe \fIidentity\fR [--effect-id \fIid\fR]
Run the kind's verifier once and write no records. Exit 0 present, 3 absent,
4 unknown. Use it for ad-hoc checks such as whether a PR merged.
.TP
.B effect verify [--with-decisions \fIaudit.jsonl\fR]
Verify the effect ledger: signatures, key windows, hash chain, index and checkpoint.
With --with-decisions, also verify the operator-decision chain and that every
linked operator decision event exists in it.
.TP
.B effect checkpoint
Sign a checkpoint and publish it to the independent sink.
.TP
.B effect kinds
List every effect kind the verifier registry holds.
.TP
.B effect keys list|init|rotate
Show ledger key IDs and public keys, provision the key in the host secret
service, or rotate it. The private key is never printed.
.TP
.B effect recover-lock [--lock \fIname\fR --authorize]
Inspect ledger locks, or remove a stale lock left by a dead writer and record
the recovery. Live, reused and unverifiable owners are refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-version, \-V
Display version information.
.TP
.B \-help, \-h
Display help information.
.TP
.B \-new \fIname\fR
Scaffold a new project with AIWG framework.
.TP
.B \-update
Update AIWG to the latest version.
.TP
.B \-status
Display health status of installed frameworks.
.TP
.B \-\-provider \fIprovider\fR
Target platform for deployment. Options: claude (default), warp, factory,
cursor, copilot, opencode, openai, windsurf.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Force overwrite existing files.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Preview changes without writing files.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Deploy SDLC framework:
.B aiwg use sdlc
.TP
Deploy to Warp Terminal:
.B aiwg use sdlc --provider warp
.TP
Scaffold new project:
.B aiwg -new my-project
.TP
Check framework status:
.B aiwg -status
.SH FRAMEWORKS
.TP
.B sdlc
Complete software development lifecycle with agents for requirements,
architecture, testing, security, and deployment.
.TP
.B marketing
Full marketing campaign management from strategy to analytics.
.TP
.B all
Deploy all available frameworks.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .aiwg/
Project artifacts directory created by AIWG commands.
.TP
.I .claude/agents/
Agent definitions for Claude Code (default provider).
.TP
.I WARP.md
Project context file for Warp Terminal provider.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AIWG_ROOT
Override the AIWG installation directory.
.TP
.B AIWG_OPENROUTER_KEY_IKEY_REFR
Provide an OpenRouter credential for a fleet key reference. The key reference
is uppercased and non-alphanumeric characters become underscores.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error.
.PP
.B aiwg effect
uses these exit codes:
.TP
.B 0
Present or recorded, including an idempotent replay, or an intact ledger.
.TP
.B 1
Internal error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
Absent.
.TP
.B 4
Unknown.
.TP
.B 5
Conflict: the same effect ID with a different payload digest, or a lock held by a live owner.
.TP
.B 6
Integrity failure.
.TP
.B 7
Artifact root unavailable; nothing was written.
